        "id": "f75-curve-2-source",
        "description": "The printed label fixes the ideal exponential with base 2. Every sampled vertex is computed as y=base^x; the shared (0,1) point is hidden, so no answer-bearing marker is added. Source-to-modern limitations: The partial side strips are symmetrically regularized to 0.25 units; this frame coordinate is a modern margin choice, not a printed endpoint value. Full source lattice lines remain at half-unit positions. Analytic curves continue only to that chosen frame; the margin is not an additional question datum.",
